2026-09-28 — NCI device prerequisite, reference control and shared runtime repair.

Historical 970-program pair: nci:nci_dev fails all eight cases on BOTH Images
at nci_dev.c:422, open("/dev/virtual_nci", O_RDWR). Those older configurations
disable NFC_VIRTUAL_NCI. The reviewed new configuration includes its module,
but the common runtime setup also needs to load it: without udev, opening an
absent device node cannot request the driver. NFC/NCI protocol autoload alone
does not register this virtual misc device.

RED: new test_virtual_nci_device_is_created_without_udev_only_when_installed
fails ([] rather than [virtual_ncidev]). The repair adds only the exact installed
drivers/nfc/virtual_ncidev.ko to the existing prerequisite list. Generic modprobe
resolves dependencies; disabled/built-in/absent module records do not invent a
preload request. Existing signed-module installation and failure checks remain.
261 K1 Python tests, targeted Ruff and git diff --check PASS. No Rust code changed.

Actual matching GCC Image/control:
  1. Load signed copies of rfkill, nfc and nci dependencies.
  2. Observe ENOENT for /dev/virtual_nci. The unchanged original exits 1,
     0/8 PASS, all eight assertions at the same missing-device line.
  3. Load the matching signed virtual_ncidev.ko. The driver registers a real
     character node; open and ioctl GET_NCIDEV_IDX succeed.
  4. Re-run the SAME original executable, same 45-second program bound:
     8/8 PASS, zero FAIL/SKIP, exit 0.
  5. Close/unload the virtual driver and all dependencies. Device disappears.
The 11 diagnostic assertions and nonce-bound boot/shutdown PASS. Parent TAP
records the two original results separately in prefixed, complete transcripts;
the expected negative original is not a PASS. The executable is byte-identical
to the retained runtime-disk original extracted with read-only debugfs.

This closes the prerequisite diagnosis and runtime packaging repair, NOT new
EvoCC module execution. That paired original replay remains required after the
uniform subject build. No old K13 totals or compiler credit are changed.

No kernel/source/installed module/disk was modified. Only four module copies
are signed using the existing matching reference key. A 13,104,640-byte
initramfs and the existing 64 MiB snapshot scratch disk are used, no new disk.
GCC14 -static -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror builds probe and existing selftest init
in evo-flight-lab:sealed, network none, one CPU/1 GiB. Readelf confirms the
unchanged original needs only the captured glibc/loader. Flight uses existing
selftest.py, hvf-host, KUnit autorun off, explicit installed-QEMU drift.

Two earlier invocations failed before starting any test because the diagnostic
list used the wrong delimiter. Their MARKERS_MISSING captures are retained as
setup-failed-*; they provide no test or boot-acceptance credit. The final list
uses the verified existing `identifier timeout` contract.

